## Why This Is Asked

Explores new angles in data privacy for IoT edge-to-cloud pipelines, focusing on end-to-end data minimization, attestation, and verifiable auditability rather than generic controls.

## Key Concepts

- Edge data minimization and in-flight redaction
- Device attestation (SPIRE) and secure TEEs for inference
- Encrypted communications (mTLS) and envelope encryption (KMS)
- ABAC for per-tenant access in cloud data lakes
- Tamper-evident logging and verifiable deletion/auditing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: redactPII at edge before forwarding
function redactPII(record){
  if(record.email) record.email = "REDACTED";
  if(record.phone) record.phone = "REDACTED";
  if(record.ssn) record.ssn = "REDACTED";
  return record;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate end-to-end privacy guarantees (tests, metrics, and audits)?
- What failure modes would you simulate, and how would incident response orchestrate recovery?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical supply-chain security skills: detection, containment, and prevention using SBOMs, provenance, reproducible builds, and policy enforcement.

## Key Concepts

- SBOMs and provenance (SLSA, Sigstore)
- Reproducible builds and attestation
- Image signing (Cosign)
- Policy gates (OPA/Gatekeeper)
- Impact assessment and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// basic attestation verification sketch
function verifyAttestation(attestation, expectedHash) {
  const crypto = require('crypto');
  const actual = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(attestation).digest('hex');
  return actual === expectedHash;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you measure blast radius after a breach?
- What changes would you make to the pipeline to prevent recurrence?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design confidential computing for multi-tenant SaaS, balancing data isolation with performance, and defining a concrete approach to revocation and incident response.

## Key Concepts
- Confidential computing (SGX/SEV) and remote attestation
- Per-tenant key management and envelope encryption
- Tamper-evident, append-only logging
- Enclave revocation, key rotation, and incident response
- Safe fallback paths and tenant dashboards exposure controls

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: verify enclave attestation before processing
async function processInEnclave(data, attestationQuote) {
  const ok = await verifyAttestation(attestationQuote);
  if (!ok) throw new Error('Attestation failed');
  return runInEnclave(data);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate enclave keys with zero-downtime across tenants?
- Compare SGX vs SEV trade-offs for this design.

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical security fundamentals at junior level with real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Rate limiting and lockout; constant-time comparisons; password hashing; MFA basics; secure logging/privacy.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo login flow illustrating bcrypt compare, MFA, and session issuance
async function login(req, res) {
  const { username, password, mfaToken } = req.body;
  const user = await getUser(username);
  if (!user) return res.status(401).send('Invalid credentials');
  const ok = await bcrypt.compare(password, user.hash);
  if (!ok) return res.status(401).send('Invalid credentials');
  if (user.mfaEnabled) {
    if (!mfaToken) return res.status(401).send('MFA required');
    const verified = speakeasy.totp.verify({ secret: user.mfaSecret, encoding: 'base32', token: mfaToken });
    if (!verified) return res.status(401).send('Invalid MFA');
  }
  const session = createSession(user.id);
  res.cookie('session', session, { httpOnly: true, secure: true });
  return res.send({ ok: true });
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt for distributed rate limiting?
- How would you test lockout and recovery flows?
- How would you store and rotate MFA seeds securely?

## Why This Is Asked

Beginner security tasks often miss logs containing PII. This question tests practical, actionable steps to prevent leakage without disrupting features.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation in logs
- PII redaction and masking
- Centralized, encrypted log sinks
- Least-privilege log access and audit trails
- CI validation for log content

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: redactPII function for logs
function redactPII(record){
  const masked = {...record};
  if (masked.email) masked.email = masked.email.replace(/[^@]+@/,'***@');
  if (masked.phone) masked.phone = masked.phone.replace(/\d(?=\d{4})/g,'*');
  return masked;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you integrate this into CI/CD and log shipping?
- How would you verify in production that no PII is emitted in logs?

